<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Table 1</span>: </span><span id="S4.T1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:113%;">Comparison for novel view synthesis on 3D scans with image &amp; video metrics.<span id="S4.T1.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <math id="S4.T1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">*</annotation></semantics></math> indicates that we fine-tuned the model on our dataset. Our method outperforms prior work and demonstrates clear effectiveness in learning accurate 3D viewpoint transformations.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S4.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21188v1/multi-views.png" id="S4.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:452/343;" width="452" height="343" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="S4.F5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Novel-view results from single-view images.<span id="S4.F5.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> HVG (ours) generates novel-view images with higher anatomic fidelity, faithfulness to input images, and consistency of geometry and texture.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
