<section id="Sx2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Appendix</h2>

<div id="Sx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this appendix, we present additional qualitative results to further illustrate the effectiveness of our approach.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Sx2.F10" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21188v1/magicanimate.png" id="Sx2.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:429/526;" width="429" height="526" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx2.F10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 10</span>: </span><span id="Sx2.F10.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Novel-view results from single-view images.<span id="Sx2.F10.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> HVG avoids the head distortions produced by MagicAnimate and predicts textures closer to the ground truth.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx2.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21188v1/animateanyone.png" id="Sx2.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/584;" width="476" height="584" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx2.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 11</span>: </span><span id="Sx2.F11.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Novel-view results from single-view images.<span id="Sx2.F11.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> HVG avoids the head distortions produced by AnimateAnyone and predicts textures closer to the ground truth.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx2.F12" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21188v1/champ.png" id="Sx2.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:476/621;" width="476" height="621" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx2.F12.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 12</span>: </span><span id="Sx2.F12.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Novel-view results from single-view images.<span id="Sx2.F12.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Compared with Champ, HVG eliminates head distortions and produces sharper, more detailed textures.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx2.F13" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21188v1/mimicmotion.png" id="Sx2.F13.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/585;" width="476" height="585" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx2.F13.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 13</span>: </span><span id="Sx2.F13.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Novel-view results from single-view images.<span id="Sx2.F13.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Compared with MimicMotion, HVG produces sharper, more detailed textures.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx2.F14" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21188v1/anigs.png" id="Sx2.F14.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:476/628;" width="476" height="628" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx2.F14.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 14</span>: </span><span id="Sx2.F14.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Novel-view results from single-view images.<span id="Sx2.F14.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> AniGS struggles to generate motion-dependent textures, whereas HVG effectively addresses this limitation and generates more clearer textures on the clothes.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx2.F15" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21188v1/lhm.png" id="Sx2.F15.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/585;" width="476" height="585" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx2.F15.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 15</span>: </span><span id="Sx2.F15.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Novel-view results from single-view images.<span id="Sx2.F15.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> LHM struggles to generate motion-dependent textures, whereas HVG effectively addresses this limitation.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx2.F16" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21188v1/magicanimate2.png" id="Sx2.F16.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:405/652;" width="405" height="652" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx2.F16.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 16</span>: </span><span id="Sx2.F16.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Novel-view novel-pose results from single-view images.<span id="Sx2.F16.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> HVG avoids the head distortions produced by MagicAnimate and predicts textures closer to the ground truth.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx2.F17" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21188v1/animateanyone2.png" id="Sx2.F17.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:405/652;" width="405" height="652" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx2.F17.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 17</span>: </span><span id="Sx2.F17.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Novel-view novel-pose results from single-view images.<span id="Sx2.F17.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> HVG avoids the head distortions produced by AnimateAnyone and predicts textures closer to the ground truth.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx2.F18" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21188v1/champ2.png" id="Sx2.F18.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:405/653;" width="405" height="653" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx2.F18.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 18</span>: </span><span id="Sx2.F18.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Novel-view novel-pose results from single-view images.<span id="Sx2.F18.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Compared with Champ, HVG produces sharper, more detailed textures.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx2.F19" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21188v1/mimicmotion2.png" id="Sx2.F19.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:405/652;" width="405" height="652" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx2.F19.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 19</span>: </span><span id="Sx2.F19.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Novel-view novel-pose results from single-view images.<span id="Sx2.F19.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Compared with MimicMotion, HVG produces sharper, more detailed textures.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx2.F20" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21188v1/anigs2.png" id="Sx2.F20.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:405/652;" width="405" height="652" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx2.F20.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 20</span>: </span><span id="Sx2.F20.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Novel-view novel-pose results from single-view images.<span id="Sx2.F20.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> AniGS struggles to generate motion-dependent textures, whereas HVG effectively addresses this limitation and generates more clearer textures on the clothes.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx2.F21" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21188v1/lhm2.png" id="Sx2.F21.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:405/652;" width="405" height="652" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx2.F21.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 21</span>: </span><span id="Sx2.F21.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Novel-view novel-pose results from single-view images.<span id="Sx2.F21.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> LHM struggles to generate motion-dependent textures, whereas HVG effectively addresses this limitation and generates more clearer textures on the clothes.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
